    <string name="feature_liturgy_mass_part_1_title">Introductory Rites</string>
    <string name="feature_liturgy_mass_part_1_text">The assembly gathers. Follow the entrance song, the greeting, the penitential act and the opening prayer.</string>
    <string name="feature_liturgy_mass_part_2_title">Liturgy of the Word</string>
    <string name="feature_liturgy_mass_part_2_text">Listen to the Scripture readings, the psalm and the Gospel. Then follow the homily and the prayer of the faithful.</string>
    <string name="feature_liturgy_mass_part_3_title">Liturgy of the Eucharist</string>
    <string name="feature_liturgy_mass_part_3_text">Follow the presentation of the gifts, the Eucharistic prayer and communion. Take part according to the guidance of the community.</string>
    <string name="feature_liturgy_mass_part_4_title">Concluding Rites</string>
    <string name="feature_liturgy_mass_part_4_text">The celebration ends with the announcements, the blessing and the dismissal to live the faith in everyday life.</string>
    <string name="feature_liturgy_mass_disclaimer">Demonstration outline to follow the celebration. The full liturgical texts must follow the official edition approved by the Church.</string>
    <string name="feature_liturgy_daily_title">Daily liturgy</string>
    <string name="feature_liturgy_daily_eyebrow">Prayer and the Word</string>
    <string name="feature_liturgy_daily_banner_description">Open missal for prayer and the liturgy</string>
    <string name="feature_liturgy_daily_card_eyebrow">To pray today</string>
    <string name="feature_liturgy_daily_card_title">The Word that gathers the community</string>
    <string name="feature_liturgy_daily_card_note">Demonstration content. The official readings must be consulted in the liturgical publications of the Church.</string>
    <string name="feature_liturgy_daily_guide_title">Prayer guide</string>
    <string name="feature_liturgy_daily_guide_badge">Guided reading</string>
    <string name="feature_liturgy_daily_step_1_title">1 · Prepare your heart</string>
    <string name="feature_liturgy_daily_step_1_text">Find a quiet moment. Make the sign of the cross and ask God to enlighten your prayer.</string>
    <string name="feature_liturgy_daily_step_2_title">2 · Word of the day</string>
    <string name="feature_liturgy_daily_step_2_text">The readings of the day will appear here once the parish connects an authorized liturgical source.</string>
    <string name="feature_liturgy_daily_step_3_title">3 · Your intention</string>
    <string name="feature_liturgy_daily_step_3_text">Present to God the joys, worries and people you want to remember today.</string>
    <string name="feature_liturgy_daily_prayer_request">Make a prayer request</string>
